\f0\b\fs28 \cf2 Annovar
\fs24 \

\f1\b0\fs20 perl-based tool for retrieving annotation information for variants in vcf file\
\

\f0\b\fs24 Installation
\fs20 \
	
\f1\b0 you have to register at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.openbioinformatics.org/annovar/annovar_download_form.php"}}{\fldrslt anovar web page }}and you will receive the install file\
	download additional databases as reference {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://annovar.openbioinformatics.org/en/latest/user-guide/download/"}}{\fldrslt here}}\
\

\f0\b\fs24 preparation
\fs20 \

\f1\b0 vfc files have to contain left-normalized indel information: ( both sample files and reference dbs)\
	$ bgzip -c sample.vcf > sample.vcf.gz			compress to gz file\
	$ tabix -p vcf file.vcf.gz					generate index file file.vcf.gz.tbi\
	$ bcftools norm -m-both -o file.step1.vcf.gz file.vcf.gz	splits multi-allelic variants into separate lines \
										(alternatively us Vt)\
	$ bcftools norm -f human_g1k_v37.fasta -o file.norm.vcf.qz	left-normalizes variants based on ref genome\
	$\
