\f0\b\fs24 general commands:
\fs20 \

\f1\b0 entry tool is table_annovar.pl\
	$ table_annovar.pl avinput <path_to_human_db> -out annofile \
		-buildver hg38					the genome build to be used - applies to all databases\

\f0\b 		
\f1\b0 -remove 						remove (and do not label) filtered variants\
		-protocol a,b,c,d 					the databases to be used\
		-operation g,r,f,f,f,f 					the operation on these databases (in same order as protocol)\
			g						gene-based annotation (genome annotation)\
			gx						gene-based with cross-reference to annotation given in -xref\
			r						region-based (if variant falls into that region, it is marked)\
			f						site-based filtering\
		-xref	<xref.txt>					add a gene-based annotation\
			xref file must have a header starting with # followed by a list of genes and their annotations\
\
		-nastring '.'\
		-csvout						for comma-separation (otherwise tab is used)\
		-vcfinput						use vcf format as input file (and output)\
									annotations are written to the info field of the vcf file (ANNOVAR_DATE=\'85ALLELE_END)\
		-polish\
			
\f0\b \
annotate_variation.pl\
	
\f1\b0 $ annotate_variation.pl\
		-geneanno / -regionanno / -filter			corresponds to the options g, r, f in table_annovar\
		-dbtype <dbname>\
		-buildver hg38\
		avinput 						the annotation will be performed and output various output files\
		<path_to_human_db>\
\

\f0\b \
\

\fs24 Input files:
\fs20 \

\f1\b0 the annovar input format is simple text file with one variant per line\
there must be five conserved columns:\
	Chromosome	Start	End	Ref	Alt\
additional columns are free and will be left alone\
	\
invalid lines are written to invalid_input and have to be checked\
\
convert2annovar.pl can convert vcf, MAQ, pileup and other into annoinput:\
	$ convert2annovar.pl -format vcf4 input -outfile avinput\
		-allsample						option to write all samples contained in a vcf to different output files\
		-includeinfo						loads all additional info from the vcf file into the avinput\
		-withzyg						also add the zytocity, quality, read coverage to avinput\
		-withfreq						prints allele frequency of each SNP based on all samples in the file\
		-comment						add the vcf header information\

\f0\b \

\f1\b0 convert2annovar can also be used to convert a list of dbSNP identifiers to annotated variants\
	$ convert2annovar.pl -format -rsid <SNP.txt> -dbsnpfile <path to dbSNP file in humandb/> -outfile snplist.txt\

\f0\b \
working with dbs in annovar:
\f1\b0 \
three different annotations:\
	- gene-based: 						give info about involved gene\
									--> RefSeq, UCSC, ENSEMBL, GENCODE\
	- region-based:						what is the context of the mutation:\
									TF-binding sites, dups, DNase hypersens..\
									-->\
	- filter-based:						variant-specific databases\
									--> SIFT, PolyPhen, dbSNP, allele freq in 1000GenomeProject\
\
\

\f0\b\fs24 Databases for annotation
\fs20 \

\f1\b0 annovar annotates varscan output using databases\
\

\f0\b loading databases:
\f1\b0 \
these have to be loaded into annovar using the following commands:\
get the databases using the downdb argument\
annotate_variation.pl -downdb -webfrom annovar		get preselected lists of dbs prepared by annovar developers\
		-downdb avdblist					get the full list of prepared dbs\
for a specific db:\
annotate_variation.pl -downdb <dbname> -buildver hg38 <path_to_humandb> \
if a specific annovar version (containing index files) exists add -webfrom annovar to command line\
annotate_variation.pl -downdb <dbname> <path_to_humandb> -buildver hg38 -webfrom annovar\
\
! vcf databases can be added via -vcfdbfile <filename> to execution of annotation (cannot be stored)\
\
\

\f0\b important dbs for exome data:\
available via -webfrom annovar:
\f1\b0 \
	dbsnfp30a							aggregation of SIFT, PolyPhen2, ..CADD, DANN, GERP++ etc.\
	dbscsnv11, spidex						splice prediction\
	clinvar							clinically relevant mutations\
	cosmic70\
	igc21								International Cancer Genome Consortium mutations\
	avsnp142							left-normalized variant of snp142 db\
\
available as -downdb <name>\
	cytoBand							\
	exac03							\
	gnomAD							genome Aggregation Database (making exac obsolete)\
										exome data from 123K individuals\
\

